# Throat — 80 bpm. A demo of the sampler's formant controls: one spoken
# phrase dropped an octave three ways.
#
# Make the reel first (any voice works; this one is the macOS system voice):
#   scripts/borrow-voice.sh "[[rate 70]] Hollow. [[slnc 200]] We are the hollow ones." renders/throat.wav Daniel
#
#   beats  0-8    the phrase at its own speed (C4 is the root)
#   beats  8-16   C3 on plain tape: half speed, and the throat drops an
#                 octave with it (the monster voice)
#   beats 16-24   C3 with `formant`: half speed, the recording's own throat
#   beats 24-32   C3 with `psola`: the pitch drops, the time and throat stay
#   beats 32-40   a melody across the keys with `formant`, the throat
#                 shrinking a fifth as it goes (smp_formant 0 -> 7)
#   beats 40-48   the voice box's own voice sings "hollow" twice on one
#                 note: as it is, then with vox_formant -7 (a bigger mouth)

bpm 80
gate 1
tail 1

automate reverb_wet
0

track natural sample=renders/throat.wav root=C4
C4:8

track tape sample=renders/throat.wav root=C4
>8 C3:8

track kept sample=renders/throat.wav root=C4 formant
>16 C3:8

track still sample=renders/throat.wav root=C4 psola
>24 C3:8

track tune sample=renders/throat.wav root=C4 formant mono
>32 C4:2 G3:2 D#3:2 C3:2
automate tune.smp_formant
0 >32 0 7:8

track mouth vox
>40 A2:4=HH-AA1-L-OW [A2]:4=HH-AA1-L-OW
automate mouth.vox_formant
0 >44 -7
automate mouth.vox_dry
1
automate mouth.vox_level
0
automate mouth.vox_vibrato
0
